// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5895 feat: addition of EDR disabling through mitigation options
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5895
// Pull request author: kurisukun
// Change: new rule
// Title: EDR Disabling With Mitigation Options Modification
// Sigma ID: 99366c3a-f4c5-4484-9eef-d74d9b003ace
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Chris Barros (Swiss Post Cybersecurity)
// Date: 2026-03-06 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-evasion, T1562.001
// Description: Detects the enablement of a mitigation option policy via registry modification. When active,
//   this policy prevents any process from loading DLLs not signed by Microsoft, breaking EDR
//   functionality that relies on vendor-signed DLL.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate custom hardening in a closed and protected environment.
//   - Windows Update modifying default mitigation configurations.
// References:
//   - https://www.orangecyberdefense.com/global/blog/cybersecurity/fairy-law
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/c7c51a25de685cd35de4c797c2bbbbf0c9267230/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_edr_disabling_with_mitigation_options.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)^HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet001\\Control\\Session Manager\\kernel.*$" and (RegistryKey contains "MitigationOptions" or RegistryKey contains "MitigationAuditOptions")) and (not((RegistryValueData in~ ("-", "(empty)"))))
